// §5.7: "The left-hand side of a procedural assignment shall be scalar,
// either an integer, real, or string identifier or an element of an
// integer, real or string array." A part-select of a `reg` is none of these
// (A.8.5 `analog_variable_lvalue` takes a variable and index expressions,
// never a range), and §7.3 writes a variable only "from the context of
// its domain". §7.3.1 Table 7-1 makes r[38:8] of a 40-bit `reg` legal to
// READ from the analog context, not to assign.
//
// The part-select target breaks A.8.5 as well as §5.7, so a tool may report
// both; `reject`, not `reject-only`.
//
// discrete_bus_part_select_above_31.va is the legal neighbour: the same
// selects of a `reg` an `initial` block sets, read in the analog block.
//
//! lrm 5.7
//! lrm 7.3
//! reject E0316
//! reject an analog procedural assignment targets an integer, real or string
//! neighbour discrete_bus_part_select_above_31.va
`include "disciplines.vams"
module ch7_discrete_bus_part_select_analog_assigned(p);
  inout p; electrical p;
  reg [39:0] r;
  analog begin
    r[38:8] = 1;
    I(p) <+ V(p);
  end
endmodule
